188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (The goal of this paper is to investigate the relationship between tourism activity in big cities and the increased resident-reported service burden, as well as whether the relationship varies across cities in order to test the assumption that increased tourism is associated with increased service/resident burden.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (This paper uses data collection, data preparation and feature construction, quantitative analysis, and visualization and tools in order to explore this relationship.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
190 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (The main objective is to analyze Google Trends and 311 service request data from city open-data portals and compare tourism activity values to tourism complaint share values for each city in order to observe how this relationship changed over time and whether trends appeared across different cities. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
191 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (Three major U.S. cities this study focuses on are Boston, Seattle, and Washington, DC. These cities experience a significant amount of tourist activity and they have a 311 service request system that is publicly accessible, making them excellent examples to analyze. Boston is useful for examining economic changes and identifying trends because it consists of dense urban areas and experiences seasonal tourism \(City of Boston, 2024\).)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E ( Seattle is growing very rapidly and experiences lots of tourism as well as environmental issues such as crowding and noise pollution \(City of Seattle, 2024\). Washington, DC attracts visitors year-round due to national landmarks and events, which provides a useful comparison to more seasonal tourism patterns. \(District of Columbia Government\).)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (Analyzing data from different cities allows for meaningful and accurate results which determine broader patterns shared across cities and whether the findings are consistent across locations.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
