/Title (However, the relationship between tourism intensity and resident service burden varies notably by city. In Boston, tourism intensity shows a moderate positive correlation with total 311 calls \(0.40\) and tourism-related calls \(0.43\), but a weaker relationship with tourism call share \(0.22\), indicating that tourism contributes to service demand without dominating complaint composition.)
